# Keep secrets and local junk OUT of the Docker build context and image layers.
# `COPY . .` in the builder stage would otherwise capture a real backend/.env (Stripe,
# Twilio, Sumsub keys) into a build layer — leaked to anyone with the layer or build cache.
#
# The `**/` variants are load-bearing, not belt-and-braces: a bare `.env`/`node_modules`
# pattern only matches at the context root, so a nested checkout (e.g. an agent worktree
# under .claude/worktrees/) would smuggle its own .env — with real keys — into a layer,
# and drag its node_modules along for the ride.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.p8
**/*.pem
**/*.p8

node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
coverage

# Local agent worktrees: full nested checkouts of this repo, none of which belong in a
# build. tsconfig.build.json's include already keeps their sources out of the program;
# this keeps them out of the context entirely.
.claude
.git
*.log
Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore
